<title>GERMANY: GRUNDIG[GRNG.CN]96 LOSS AROUND 350 MLN DM - SOURCE.</title>
<headline>GRUNDIG[GRNG.CN]96 LOSS AROUND 350 MLN DM - SOURCE.</headline>
<dateline>FUERTH, Germany 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>German electronics maker Grundig AG [GRNG.CN] lost about 350 million marks in 1996, on sales of 3.3 billion to 3.4 billion marks, sources close to the troubled firm told Reuters.</p>
<p>Philips NV , which ran Grundig until its contract with the Max Grundig Foundation expired January 1, would bear the loss, the source said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
